    "upstream_operation": "ACVP-AES-KW 1.0 and ACVP-AES-KWP 1.0 AFT (SP 800-38F key wrap with the forward cipher); decrypt groups carry upstream testPassed=false integrity failures. Each testGroup names its own upstream file",
    "local_operation": "encrypt: C_CreateObject(generic secret, CKA_VALUE = pt, extractable) + C_WrapKey(CKM_AES_KEY_WRAP | CKM_AES_KEY_WRAP_KWP, default IV) under the imported KEK, output byte-compared to ct; decrypt: C_UnwrapKey(ct) into a generic secret, its CKA_VALUE byte-compared to pt for testPassed=true; for testPassed=false C_UnwrapKey must refuse (no object)",
    "transformation": "subset only; every retained field is byte-copied from the upstream files (hex case preserved); no value is re-derived",
    "subset_policy": "Deterministic. kwCipher=cipher groups only. Payload lengths: KW the shortest and longest registered (128 and 4096 bits, 64-bit aligned); KWP the shortest (8 bits, one byte) and the longest non-64-bit-aligned (3040 bits = 380 bytes, padding path). Per file x key length (128/192/256) x those two payload lengths: encrypt -> the lowest-tcId case; decrypt -> the lowest-tcId testPassed=true case, plus for the shorter payload the lowest-tcId testPassed=false case. kwCipher=inverse groups (KW-AE/KWP-AE with the inverse cipher) are listed in notExecuted: PKCS#11 v3.2 has no mechanism for them.",
    "retained_fields": "tcId, testPassed, key, pt, ct (pt of a testPassed=false case is carried but not used)",
    "negative_classes_upstream": ["decrypt with testPassed=false (integrity check fails)"]
  },
